<title>UK: FOCUS-British train franchise faces big fine.</title>
<headline>FOCUS-British train franchise faces big fine.</headline>
<byline>Edna Fernandes</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British railway franchise South West Trains, a unit of Stagecoach Plc, faced the threat of a one million pound ($1.6 million) fine and the loss of its licence on Friday in a regulatory bite-back after it cancelled 2,543 trains in eight weeks.</p>
<p>South West Trains (SWT), which mainly operates commuter services into London, has cancelled numerous services after job reductions left it with too few drivers to operate new shift patterns.</p>
